/*
:name: aeg_mux_lane_writes_2
:type: lec
:set: compile.cprop.engine=aegraph compile.aegraph.cost=sim
:compile_grep: aegraph-rule mux_setmask_arm tried=[0-9]+ matched=[1-9][0-9]* applied=[1-9][0-9]* extracted=0
*/
// HEADER-ONLY variant: aeg_mux_lane_writes.prp compiled by the e-graph engine under the `sim` cost profile. The lane
// factoring is an alt (mux_setmask_arm: `Mux(s, b, Set_mask(b, w, v))` = `Set_mask(b, w, Mux(s, Get_mask(b, w), v))`):
// hardware pays per bit, so the default `synth` profile takes the narrow lane Mux (aeg_mux_lane_writes_1), but a
// simulator word is a word and the factored form adds a Get_mask, so `sim` keeps the word Mux of a register of at
// most 64 bits. The rule still fires (matched, applied) and the extraction does not take it (extracted=0).
// The result must still prove equal to the classic reference.
